"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_010_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "10", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/14"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_011_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "11", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/15"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/16"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/17"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/18"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "19", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/19"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "20", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/20"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "21", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/21"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_018_thumb.jpg", "page": "22", "label": "18", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/22"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_019_thumb.jpg", "page": "23", "label": "[19]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/23"}, {"image": "/11909/11909_ms16800_1_14_020_thumb.jpg", "page": "24", "label": "[20]", "href": "/paper-summary/ordinance-14-november-1842/24"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "ordinance-14-november-1842", "series": "JSPPA", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPA6", "documentSeriesIdCompiled": "jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesUri": "/the-papers/administrative-records/jsppa6/jsppa6-sub-nccr/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02/jsppa6-sub-nccr-sub02-421114", "documentSeriesTitle": "<p>\r\n\tMeeting, 14 November 1842</p>", "editorialPageNumber": "16", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/54016763/54016763-0020.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> one thousand Dollars and not less than five hundred Dollars <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16771336512436457967\"><a href=\"#16771336512436457967\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans32\"><span id=\"documenttrans32\">32</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The 1827 statute stated that delinquent officers should be penalized with “a sum not exceeding five hundred dollars, and shall be incapable of holding or executing his said office.” (An Act . . . on Writs of Habeas Corpus, p. 326, sec. 13.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">The Revised Code of Laws, of Illinois, Enacted at the Fifth General Assembly, at Their Session Held at Vandalia, Commencing on the Fourth Day of December, 1826, and Ending the Nineteenth of February, 1827.</span> Vandalia, IL: Robert Blackwell, 1827.</p></div></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 12— Any Person or Persons having a Prisoner or Prisoners in his or their custody or under his or their restraint, power or controul for whose relief a writ or Writs of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16138769332166683725\"><a href=\"#16138769332166683725\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> is issued, who with intent to avoid the effect of such writ or Writs shall transfer such person or Persons to the Custody of or place him her or them under the control of <span class=\"underscore\">any other</span> Person or Persons, or shall conceal him her or them, or change the place of his her or their confinement, with intent to avoid the operation of such writ or writs or with intent to remove him her or them out of the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"11939425377125048760\"><a href=\"#11939425377125048760\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6189\" place=\"x6189\" title=\"Illinois\">State</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Illinois\"><p>Became part of Northwest Territory of U.S., 1787. Admitted as state, 1818. Population in 1840 about 480,000. Population in 1845 about 660,000. Plentiful, inexpensive land attracted settlers from northern and southern states. Following expulsion from Missouri...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>, shall forfeit for every such offence one thousand Dollars and may be imprisoned not less then one year nor more<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16942146092724303267\"><a href=\"#16942146092724303267\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans22\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> then five years, In any prosectution for the penalty incurred under this section, it shall not be necessary to shew that the writ or Writs of Habeas Corpus [p. 16]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> one thousand Dollars and not less than five hundred <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>Dollars <span class=\"deleted\">and</span> <span class=\"deleted\">shall</span> <span class=\"deleted\">be</span> <span class=\"deleted\">incapable</span> <span class=\"deleted\">of</span> <span class=\"deleted\">holding</span> <span class=\"deleted\">or</span> <span class=\"deleted\">executing</span> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"deleted\">his</span> <span class=\"deleted\">said</span> <span class=\"deleted\">office,</span><aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"13275277088179673224\"><a href=\"#13275277088179673224\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans32\"><span id=\"documenttrans32\">32</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">The 1827 statute stated that delinquent officers should be penalized with “a sum not exceeding five hundred dollars, and shall be incapable of holding or executing his said office.” (An Act . . . on Writs of Habeas Corpus, p. 326, sec. 13.)</p><hr><div class=\"works-cited-links\"><a href=\"/works-cited\" class=\"pdf\" id=\"comp-works\">Comprehensive Works Cited</a></div><div class=\"source-note\"><p id=\"source-note1\"><span class=\"title\">The Revised Code of Laws, of Illinois, Enacted at the Fifth General Assembly, at Their Session Held at Vandalia, Commencing on the Fourth Day of December, 1826, and Ending the Nineteenth of February, 1827.</span> Vandalia, IL: Robert Blackwell, 1827.</p></div></div></div></aside></div> <div class=\"indent wasptag\">Section 12— Any <span class=\"deleted\">one</span> &lt;​Person or Persons​&gt; having a <span class=\"deleted\">person</span> &lt;​Prisoner or Prisoners​&gt; in his &lt;​or their​&gt; custody or <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>under his &lt;​or their​&gt; restraint, power or controul for whose <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>relief a writ &lt;​or Writs​&gt; of <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4951217461180681785\"><a href=\"#4951217461180681785\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x41899\" topic=\"x41899\" title=\"Habeas corpus\">Habeas Corpus</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Habeas corpus\"><p>“Have the body”; a written order from a court of competent jurisdiction commanding anyone having a person in custody to produce such person at a certain time and place and to state the reasons why he or she is being held in custody. The court will determine...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/topic/habeas-corpus\">View Glossary</a></div></div></aside> is issued, who with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>intent to avoid the effect of such writ &lt;​or Writs​&gt; shall transfer <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>such person &lt;​or Persons​&gt; to the Custody &lt;​of​&gt; or place him <span class=\"deleted\">or</span> her &lt;​or them​&gt; under <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>the control of <span class=\"underscore\">any other</span> &lt;​Person or Persons,​&gt; or shall conceal him &lt;​her​&gt; or <span class=\"deleted\">her</span> &lt;​them​&gt;, <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>or change the place of <span class=\"deleted\">him</span> &lt;​his​&gt; &lt;​her​&gt; or <span class=\"deleted\">her</span> &lt;​their​&gt; confinement, with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>intent to avoid the operation of such writ &lt;​or writs​&gt; or with <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>intent to remove him &lt;​her​&gt; or <span class=\"deleted\">her</span> &lt;​them​&gt; out of the <aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"12899061703818181525\"><a href=\"#12899061703818181525\" class=\"reference staticPopup\" ro=\"x6189\" place=\"x6189\" title=\"Illinois\">State</a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data\" isnote=\"Y\" isnonsearchable=\"Y\"><input type=\"hidden\" value=\"Illinois\"><p>Became part of Northwest Territory of U.S., 1787. Admitted as state, 1818. Population in 1840 about 480,000. Population in 1845 about 660,000. Plentiful, inexpensive land attracted settlers from northern and southern states. Following expulsion from Missouri...</p><a class=\"more\" href=\"/place/illinois\">More Info</a></div></div></aside>, shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>forfeit for every such offence one thousand Dollars <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and may be imprisoned not less then one year nor <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span><span class=\"deleted\">less</span> &lt;​more​&gt;<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"552479863738846196\"><a href=\"#552479863738846196\" class=\"new-scribe-note staticPopup\" title=\"New Scribe\" name=\"trans22\"><img src=\"//cdn.churchofjesuschrist.org/ch/jsp/images/icn-new-scribe-16.png\" alt=\"Indicates a change in handwriting to a different scribe.\"></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">Insertion in the handwriting of first unidentified scribe.</p><hr></div></div></aside> then five years, In any prosectution for the <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>penalty incurred under this section, it shall not be <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>necessary to shew that the writ &lt;​or Writs​&gt; of Habeas Corpus [p. 16]</div></body></html>", "calendars